; Item: step the frame animation, then queue the item's sprite
;
; The common tail of the item actions whose sprite is animated and depends on nothing else (#R$A6D8, #R$A70B). The
; wheel crosses (#R$A782, #R$A7B1) do the same with a frame offset of their own and enter at #R$A7D9. Entered with SP
; at slot + 8: the caller has popped the flag pointer. Pops the animation words of the slot (+8: C = countdown, B =
; reload value; +$A: E = frame, D = number of frames); the countdown goes down by one and at zero it reloads from B,
; the frame goes up by one and wraps to 0 at D. #R$A7D9 then stores the words back and #R$A7DB queues the sprite of
; frame A.
; .
; Hardware: none; the sprite is only queued (#R$ACE5), the screen is written later.
;
; SP Slot address + 8 (the flag pointer is already popped)
@label=AnimateItem
c$A7CB POP BC        ; C = countdown, B = reload
 $A7CC POP DE        ; E = frame, D = number of frames
 $A7CD LD A,E        ; A = frame
 $A7CE DEC C         ;
 $A7CF JR NZ,$A7D9   ; countdown not over
 $A7D1 LD C,B        ; reload; next frame, wrapping at D
 $A7D2 INC A         ;
 $A7D3 LD E,A        ;
 $A7D4 CP D          ;
 $A7D5 JR C,$A7D9    ;
 $A7D7 SUB D         ;
 $A7D8 LD E,A        ;
; Entry point of #R$A7CB, #R$A782 and #R$A7B1: A = frame to draw, DE and BC = the animation words to put back into the
; slot
@label=AnimateItem_Store
*$A7D9 PUSH DE       ; store the animation words back
 $A7DA PUSH BC       ;
